1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,900
Hi, we're team CampusConnect: Salama, Aro, Makar and Omar.

2
00:00:06,220 --> 00:00:09,860
CampusConnect is a social network for the MBZUAI community,

3
00:00:09,860 --> 00:00:12,400
where students and groups share updates in one feed.

4
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:16,100
This proof of concept shows one interaction end to end: creating a post.

5
00:00:16,340 --> 00:00:19,200
The browser sends POST /posts,

6
00:00:19,320 --> 00:00:22,800
FastAPI validates it, and the post appears in the feed.

7
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:28,600
You can see that when we refresh, it's blank.

8
00:00:29,120 --> 00:00:32,200
So the feed is empty. On load, the page calls GET /posts,

9
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:35,700
gets an empty list, and shows no error.

10
00:00:35,900 --> 00:00:39,060
Now let's create a post. You can see we created this post,

11
00:00:39,060 --> 00:00:42,200
and when we refresh, it's still there.

12
00:00:42,580 --> 00:00:44,900
The backend returns 201 Created.

13
00:00:44,900 --> 00:00:50,560
Let's add another post. As you can see, the newer post is on top,

14
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:55,300
and no posts disappear when we refresh, because they're in the backend.

15
00:00:55,640 --> 00:00:59,800
Now if we try blank spaces, it shows us an error:

16
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:05,000
a 422 error. The string should have at least one character.

17
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:10,400
So nothing is stored.

18
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:14,600
We found this gap during the requirements review and fixed it with a test.

19
00:01:18,460 --> 00:01:21,900
Now let's move on to the docs.

20
00:01:22,580 --> 00:01:24,500
This is our API contract.

21
00:01:24,620 --> 00:01:28,000
The request has an author of up to 100 characters

22
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:31,000
and content of up to 1,000.

23
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:36,200
The 201 response adds an id and created_at.

24
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:42,800
Errors use FastAPI's standard 422 shape, which the frontend reads.

25
00:01:43,660 --> 00:01:47,180
The schema is generated from the same Pydantic models as the code,

26
00:01:47,180 --> 00:01:50,900
and eight backend tests check status codes, ordering and error shapes.

27
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:53,600
The POC is deliberately small.

28
00:01:53,740 --> 00:01:59,100
We use plain HTML and JavaScript instead of React.

29
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:03,800
There's no sign-in, so the author is free text.

30
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:07,860
Posts live in memory instead of PostgreSQL, and every post is public.

31
00:02:07,860 --> 00:02:11,720
In Assignment 2 we add university sign-in, PostgreSQL,

32
00:02:11,720 --> 00:02:16,280
groups with audience control, live updates over WebSockets, moderation

33
00:02:16,280 --> 00:02:19,000
and AI thread summaries.

34
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:22,200
Setup instructions are in the README on GitHub.

35
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:24,500
Thank you!
